// Warhammer 40,000 11th edition – the 45 terrain layouts of the Warhammer Event Companion (Games Workshop,
// version of 14 Oct 2026, pages 9–53): three layouts (A/B/C) for each pairing of Force Dispositions. Extracted from
// the PDF: deployment zones and objectives from the vector graphics; every terrain area and every terrain feature from
// the card's image placements (centre and rotation exact to the artwork, sizes snapped to the Battlefields: Armageddon
// footprints 6"×2", 6"×4", 7"×11.5", 10"×2.5" and the 8"×11.5" polygon).
// Battlefield 44" (x) × 60" (y), Attacker's edge at y = 0, like data/rules.js. Each layout carries its own deployment
// zones (polygons), objectives (home a / home d / central / expansion – all inside terrain areas) and the 15 terrain
// areas with their class: tall = dense (green on the card, blocks line of sight), low = light (yellow, cover only).
// Pieces with a `poly` are irregular footprints: outline points relative to (x, y), already in table orientation.
//
// A terrain area (the grey plate on the card) is made of individual terrain features placed on it – that is what the
// players put on the table: green = dense ruin parts (the L-shaped ruin sections, labelled AB/CD/EF/GH on the card),
// yellow = light cover (barricades, low wall pieces); some areas combine both (two barricades + a pipe junction).
//   parts: [{ t, k, x, y, rot, flip, label }] – t = key into PARTS11, k = 'dense' | 'light', x/y = the feature's centre
//   relative to the area's centre in TABLE orientation (not rotated with the area), rot = degrees clockwise,
//   flip = mirrored artwork (mirror the template's y before rotating), label = the card's letters on dense parts.
//   PARTS11[t] = { kind, w, h, poly: [[[x, y], …], …] } – the feature's outline(s) in inches, centred, unrotated.
// Source PDF: https://assets.warhammer-community.com/eng_14-10_wh40k_event_companion-rdwnqprl4c-nj8oqogadv.pdf

